%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI can't seem to figure out exactly what you aim to gain\nfrom this.\d%K%P
「你的目的到底是什么，无论如何我都搞不懂」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dOh?\d%K%P
「啊啦」%K%P
Her feminine eyebrows twitched slightly.%K%P
在我面前一直是一副大小姐姿态的她，\n微微地翘了翘眉毛。%K%P
I couldn't tell if she was surprised by the fact I hit the\nnail on the head, or simply exasperated by my stupidity.%K%P
那副表情，既像是对我意外的发言而感到惊讶，\n又像是期待落空而稍显无措般，有种微妙的感觉。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI've heard rumors about your father -- how his approach\nto business tends to be somewhat extreme for such a large\ncompany.\d%K%P
「关于你父亲经营的公司，我听过很多的传闻。\n那个，对于那么大型的企业来讲，稍显过激的事情…」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dHmm?\d%K%P
「哼嗯～？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAnd with that in mind, I find your approach here a bit\ntoo soft.\d%K%P
「然后，综合了这些传闻想想看的话，\n我觉得你所进行的交涉，对于泽嶋房地产而言\n不是过于幼稚了么」%K%P
That was what bothered me the most.%K%P
没错，这就是最大的违和感。%K%P
I didn't mean to be rude, but for a company known for its\ncruelty, her way of playing this was almost ridiculously\nsoft.%K%P
虽然话说得难听了点，\n相比败德房地产商那些厚颜无耻的手段而言，\n再幼稚也不会这样。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYour conditions are too good. I mean, I probably\nshouldn't be saying this, but we're all problematic\ntenants. You could find a million ways to evict us if you\nwanted.\d%K%P
「老实说，这条件过于优厚了。\n毕竟我们几个，硬说的话就是不良住户。\n能够把我们赶出去的口实，应该要多少有多少」%K%P
Compensations, relocation support, and the present\nroundabout way of trying to ruin my reputation -- her\nseemingly calculating tone sheltered hint after hint of\npure naivete.%K%P
对租户的补偿，对业主的关照，再加上这次的曝光事件。\n与冷彻的风评背道而驰，她接二连三地使出了种种怀柔手段。%K%P
I simply couldn't see her having the heart to set a trap\nthat would cheat us out of our property and leave us\nwandering the streets, penniless.%K%P
巧妙地布设陷阱，等待时机趁虚而入，\n然后理所当然地兼并这里的土地，一毛钱也不多花之类，\n完全感觉不出她会那样去做的迹象。%K%P
...Besides, we were all penniless and powerless to begin\nwith.%K%P
…毕竟这里的住户们，含我在内，都穷得身无一文。%K%P
And...%K%P
而且…%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAnd one more thing. Why are you so nice to Mitoko?\d%K%P
「还有一点…\n为什么要对美都子，那么温柔呢？」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
She appeared right in front of Mitoko when she was at her\nworst. And even if that was just an act, it still ended up\ngiving her ample support.%K%P
这个人，在孤立无援而惶恐不安的美都子面前出现，\n就算只是表面装样子也罢，\n她事实上也的确成为了美都子的心灵支柱。%K%P
Besides, the Mitoko I knew was a shrewd and careful girl.\nShe wouldn't blindly fall victim to makeshift kindness.\n...Probably.%K%P
而且，那样一个聪颖机敏、头脑灵光的好孩子，\n对心存不轨接近自己的大人是一定会感到不安的\n…我是这么觉得。%K%P
The \dsoftness\d this girl was showing to us tenants was of\na completely different sort compared to the \dkindness\d she\ndisplayed around Mitoko.%K%P
给其他住户的『甜头』，\n和对美都子的『温柔』，\n有着本质上的不同。%K%P
She was offering us money and riches without a second\nthought, but in the case of our landlord, she was going\nout of her way to do things that made no sense whatsoever\nfrom a business perspective.%K%P
对我们是用令人绝不会感到惋惜的大量金钱对付过去，\n但是对美都子则是完全付出真心的呵护%K%P
She gained her trust by talking to her time and again,\ndropped everything and flew all the way to Japan just for\nher, and brought thoughtful -- but not necessarily\nexpensive -- presents.%K%P
不断接触而获得了信赖，一听说有困难立刻就飞到身边，\n还不忘带尽管没有多昂贵，却讨人喜欢的特产来。%K%P
If that was all an act, she was no longer a mere\nbusinesswoman, but a grade A scammer at this point.%K%P
要是为了蒙骗能做到这地步…\n那个人就不是一流的房地产商，而是一流的欺诈师了。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dFrom my point of view, it doesn't seem like you're just\ndoing this for the land. I can't help but feel that you\nmight have...\d%K%P
「我无论如何也不相信你只是为了那块地而这样做。\n一定还有些别的什么…」%K%P
